Begin
Title:          GRUMMP
Version:        0.5.0
Entered-date:   100218
Description:    GRUMMP is a toolkit for Generation and Refinement of
                Unstructured Mixed-element Meshes in Parallel.  (At this
                point, the "Mixed-element" and "Parallel" parts of the
                name are still statements of intent rather than
                reality.)  The toolkit includes executables for
                unstructured mesh generation, improvement, and
                coarsening in both two and three dimensions, as well as
                interpolation of scattered data.  The underlying
                libraries on which the executables are built are
                included, but the API is not yet documented for public
                use, and is subject to significant change.
Keywords:       triangular mesh generation, tetrahedral mesh generation,
                unstructured meshes, mesh improvement, mesh quality,
                mesh coarsening for multigrid
Author:         cfog@mech.ubc.ca (Dr. Carl Ollivier-Gooch)
Maintained-by:  cfog@mech.ubc.ca (Dr. Carl Ollivier-Gooch)
Primary-site:   tetra.mech.ubc.ca /pub/GRUMMP
                ~1800kB GRUMMP.tar.gz
Alternate-site: http://tetra.mech.ubc.ca/GRUMMP
Copying-policy: Freely available for non-profit use.  See enclosed license.
End
